    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py` and wrote a 52-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The function validates `order_by`, `limit` and `offset` before querying, then runs one parameterised, read-only SELECT. Out-of-stock rows are filtered by `stock > 0`, and name matching uses `INSTR(LOWER(...))` rather than `LIKE`, so `%` and `_` are literal. Ties are broken by `id` ascending in both directions, and each result is a plain `{id, name, price}` dict even when the connection has a `row_factory` set. Two choices go beyond the spec: `bool` values are rejected for `limit` and `offset`, and case-insensitivity follows SQLite's `LOWER()`, which is ASCII-only unless the ICU extension is loaded. While tightening the tests I corrected several of my own wrong expectations before the run, so the passing suite reflects the spec rather than the first draft. No other files were created and no packages were installed.",
